===Week 3: Guilty Pleasures Night===
The couples performed one unlearned dance to a song that reminded them of their secret guilty pleasure. Couples are listed in the order they performed.

At the start of the show, a moment of silence was held to honor the victims of the [[2017 Las Vegas shooting]], which had occurred the previous day.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2017/tv/news/las-vegas-shooting-dancing-with-the-stars-moment-of-silence-1202578332/|title='Dancing With the Stars' to Open With Moment of Silence to Honor Las Vegas Shooting Victims|last=Otterson|first=Joe|work=Variety|date=October 2, 2017|access-date=October 2, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171003014042/http://variety.com/2017/tv/news/las-vegas-shooting-dancing-with-the-stars-moment-of-silence-1202578332/|archive-date=October 3, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> It was announced at the beginning of the show that, due to the tragedy, no elimination would take place.

[[Vanessa Lachey]] performed with [[Alan Bersten]] this week while [[Maksim Chmerkovskiy]] was absent dealing with a "personal matter".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Seemayer |first=Zach |date=October 2, 2017 |title=Alan Bersten Steps in for Maks Chmerkovskiy on 'DWTS' as the Pro Deals With a 'Personal Issue' |url=https://www.etonline.com/alan-bersten-steps-in-for-maks-chmerkovskiy-on-dwts-as-the-pro-deals-with-a-personal-issue-88459 |access-date=September 12, 2023 |website=Entertainment Tonight |language=en-US |archive-date=October 17, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231017104555/https://www.etonline.com/alan-bersten-steps-in-for-maks-chmerkovskiy-on-dwts-as-the-pro-deals-with-a-personal-issue-88459 |url-status=live }}</ref>

